From 466698d250d5e23131ad5df490eb35b602f4c0e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:10:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Show menus and tooltips as popups placed by the
 compositor.

A Wayland client cannot choose where a window goes, so a menu or tooltip
that does not belong to a window with a surface, such as the menu of a
tray icon, appeared wherever the compositor liked. Show those windows
as an xdg_popup anchored to an output with xx_output_popup_v1, or as a
wlr-layer-shell surface when that is missing. Compositors with neither
keep showing them as toplevels.
